  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Commerce has obligated $3.5B in contracts in FY2026 to date. The agency issued 6,702 awards with an average award size of $515K. Obligations fell 16.9% year over year. Historical obligations show variation: FY21 was $4.5B, FY22 was $4.1B, FY23 was $5B, FY24 was $5.2B, and FY25 was $4.2B. Technology services dominate FY2026 to date spending, led by Other Computer Related Services at $639M and Computer Systems Design Services at $515M. Professional and technical services, publishing, ship building and repair, and aircraft manufacturing also appear in the top NAICS categories. REED TECHNOLOGY AND INFORMATION SERVICES LLC is the largest contractor by obligations at $218M, followed by ACCENTURE FEDERAL SERVICES LLC at $111M and LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION at $108M. The FY2026 to date totals are partial because they cover the fiscal year to date only.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2026 contract spending compare to prior years?",
        "body": "The Department of Commerce obligated $3.5B in FY2026 to date. FY26 obligations are lower than FY25, which were $4.2B, and also lower than FY24, which were $5.2B. FY23 obligations were $5B, FY22 obligations were $4.1B, and FY21 obligations were $4.5B."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which industries and vendors account for the largest shares of Commerce contracts?",
        "body": "Other Computer Related Services is the largest category at $639M, followed by Computer Systems Design Services at $515M and Custom Computer Programming Services at $362M. REED TECHNOLOGY AND INFORMATION SERVICES LLC is the top vendor at $218M, followed by ACCENTURE FEDERAL SERVICES LLC at $111M and LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION at $108M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Department of Commerce spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of Commerce has obligated $3.5B in contracts in FY2026 to date. The agency issued 6,702 awards with an average award size of $515K. Obligations fell 16.9% year over year, and the fiscal year to date totals are partial."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Commerce buy?",
      "a": "Commerce buys services and products led by Other Computer Related Services at $639M, Computer Systems Design Services at $515M, and Custom Computer Programming Services at $362M. Commerce also buys publishing services at $220M, ship building and repairing at $149M, and a range of professional, technical, surveying, and engineering services."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are Commerce's largest contractors?",
      "a": "Commerce's largest contractors by obligations are REED TECHNOLOGY AND INFORMATION SERVICES LLC at $218M, ACCENTURE FEDERAL SERVICES LLC at $111M, and LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION at $108M. Other top vendors include JAG KETCHIKAN, LLC at $99.6M, EARTH RESOURCES TECHNOLOGY, LLC at $98M, and BOOZ ALLEN HAMILTON INC at $95.9M."
